# Extended-UniVRM repository

- Target Unity `2022.3.62f2`; do not silently raise Unity, package, API compatibility,
  or C# language requirements.
- Keep changes in the owning package: `Packages/UniGLTF`, `Packages/VRM`, or
  `Packages/VRM10`. Use its `Runtime`, `Editor`, `Tests`, or `Samples~` folder.
- Select namespace and dependencies from nearby code and the nearest `.asmdef`.
  There is no single repository root namespace.
- Runtime assemblies must not reference Editor assemblies or `UnityEditor`.
  Put editor-only code under an `Editor` folder and editor-only asmdef.
- When crossing an assembly boundary, update the owning `.asmdef` deliberately.
  Avoid adding broad or circular references.
- Preserve supported VRM/glTF behavior, serialized data, and public API compatibility.
  Avoid unrelated cleanup in legacy files.
- Do not modify package copies under `Assets/` when the authoritative source is under
  `Packages/`; identify the owning source before editing duplicated-looking code.
